{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicIsometryInversion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicIsometryInversion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Euclidean.Inversion.Calculus"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dH_boundaryInversion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dH_boundaryInversion","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicIsometryInversion.lean#L88-L95","doc":"**C2 — inversion in a boundary sphere preserves the hyperbolic distance.**\nFor a centre `c` on the boundary `∂H³` (`c_z = 0`) and radius `R > 0`, the\ninversion `EuclideanGeometry.inversion c R` is a `dH`-isometry — DERIVED from the\nconformal-height-scaling engine (`IsDHIsometry.dH_eq`), not adopted; the inversion\nis involutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.boundaryInversionIsom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.boundaryInversionIsom","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicIsometryInversion.lean#L41-L86","doc":"**The conformal height-scaling data of a boundary inversion.**  On `H³` (where\n`p ≠ c`), the inversion's Fréchet derivative is `(R/‖p-c‖)²·(orthogonal\nreflection)` — a positive scalar times a linear isometry — so it scales every\ntangent norm by `lam(p) = (R/‖p-c‖)²`, and (because `c_z = 0`) it scales the\nheight by the SAME factor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}